#. translators: Name of an ability an AI assistant or an MCP client can use on the store.
#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:88
msgid "Move products from a custom attribute to a global one"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: the most variations a product may have to be moved.
#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:90
#, php-format
msgid "Moves products from a custom product attribute to a global one: the product's attribute with its position, visibility and use for variations, its default choice, every variation's value, and the Pixonaut form arrangements naming the attribute. Each product is written as one, so customers never see it part-way, and each variation keeps its id, price, image and Pixonaut setup. Links and cart lines naming the old attribute go on selecting the same value. Create the global attribute and its terms first; a value matches a term by name or slug, or by `term_map`. Each product's `before` records its state before the move, including any stored setup it renames; run it with `dry_run` first and keep the answer. It is a record, not an undo: no ability restores it, and going back means `update-product`, `update-product-variation`, and `set-product-setup` with the sides' `form_groups`. A product with more than %d variations is refused. Without `product_ids` it walks the store's products a page at a time; call again with the next page while `more` is true."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:96
msgid "The custom attribute, by its name or slug, e.g. `Size`."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:101
msgid "The global attribute, by its slug with or without `pa_`, e.g. `pa_size`."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:106
msgid "For a value not named as its term: the term's name or slug, by the value."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:111
msgid "Say what would happen, with a record of each product's state in `before`, and change nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:116
msgid "Only these products; left out to walk them all."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:125
msgid "The page of the store's products, from 1."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:187
msgid "No global attribute has this slug. Create it with create-product-attribute first."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:211
msgid "The store's products could not be read."
msgstr ""

#: src/Abilities/MoveProductAttribute.php:244
#: src/Abilities/ProductLinks.php:91
